# colcon's output is ignored by the repository's top-level .gitignore, along
# with the rest of the ROS artefacts. This file exists for the other half of
# the problem: that .gitignore is written for a Python project, and three of
# its patterns would drop files this workspace needs.

# `*.txt` (kept for requirements.txt only) would drop every package manifest.
!**/CMakeLists.txt

# `tests/` and `test*` would drop the test directories and every test file.
!**/test/
!**/test/**
!**/test_*.py

# ...but not the caches pytest leaves behind in them.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
